Z||000002||Oreif||06-25-2000||06:39 AM||||I don't know if they make it anymore but I think "scoushe" (??) use to make a plate that would hold 2 4" round speakers and fill a 4X10 hole. It was originally designed for the older GM luxury cars (late 70's early 80's. I don't remember where I saw them, maybe in an old Car Stereo magazine. If they don't make it anymore maybe one of our more industrious members could come up with one?||||reg||1
Z||000003||chris6878||06-25-2000||12:15 PM||||i want high quality speakers,  what would ya recommend?    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||3
Z||000004||stillofknight||06-25-2000||11:13 PM|||| Try Radio Shack for some 4x10 adapter plates.  You have to ask for their car audio book that has Scocshe in it.  I was there Sat. and saw it.  I forget if they had 4x10's though.||||reg||1
Z||000005||stillofknight||06-25-2000||11:15 PM||||Oh, and as for quality, look for MB Quart, Focal, Diamond Audio, Boston Acoustics, ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Patrick's Dad||06-25-2000||11:16 PM||||There is only one recommendation.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.diamondaudio.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.diamondaudio.com</A> <P>I've been lusting after the S400a HEX 4" components, with the MacDaddy 8.4 subs to back them up. Just looking at the workmanship of the crossover is enough to make you weak in the knees (If you really like your music).  You'll need a real audio amp if you're looking at these. Probably the only one to look at is MacIntosh.<P>If you don't want to spend *that* much, look at MbQuart. Best sound I've heard on a reasonable budget (My definition of "reasonable budget": On par with what you'd spend on Alpine, good Pioneer, and the like.)||||reg||1
Z||000007||1FST2M6||06-26-2000||08:21 AM||||I've got 2 sets of MB Quart 4" CoAxial. driven buy decent Kenwood KAC-626. I made the plate out of  1/4" fiberboard. backed by an Xtant 1001dx and 10" Kicker solobaric..i I had a set of Pioneer 3 ways for a couple day and wasn't able to get any decent clairity. after their replacement with the current set-up I can drive then as loud as i want with no audible distortion.. you can see it on a Q meter at a decent Stereo shop (any IASCA event) .  When puting in 4" speakers make sure your have a good crossover.. like the MB Quart, DiamondAudio, etc. if you don't you'll kill them a lot faster than the stock 4x10... ||||reg||1
Z||000008||phillip||06-26-2000||08:49 AM||||i've gotten a few good deals on infinity reference series speakers. might want to check around.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by phillip (edited 06-26-2000).]||||reg||1
